-- luanti/doc/lua_api.md: Textures

--[[
A texture name or texture string with optional modifiers.

Mods should prefix textures with `modname_`, e.g. `foomod_foothing.png`.
The file extension may be omitted (`foomod_foothing`). Supported formats are
PNG (`.png`), JPEG (`.jpg`) and Targa (`.tga`).

**Overlaying:** join textures with `^`; the right-hand texture is drawn on top.
* `default_dirt.png^default_grass_side.png`

**Grouping:** enclose in `(` and `)`.
* `cobble.png^(thing1.png^thing2.png)`

**Modifiers:** start with `[` and are generated by the client on the fly,
applied in sRGB colorspace (no gamma correction).
* `[crack:<vertical_frames>:<crack_frame>`, `[cracko:...`
  (both also accept `<grid>` before `<vertical_frames>`)
* `[combine:<w>x<h>:<x>,<y>=<texture>:<x>,<y>=<texture>...`
* `[resize:<w>x<h>`
* `[opacity:<ratio>` (0-255)
* `[invert:<mode>` (`r`, `g`, `b`, `a`)
* `[brighten`
* `[noalpha`
* `[makealpha:<r>,<g>,<b>`
* `[transform<t>` (`I`, `R90`, `R180`, `R270`, `FX`, `FY`, ...)
* `[inventorycube{<top>{<left>{<right>`
* `[fill:<w>x<h>:<x>,<y>:<color>`
* `[lowpart:<percent>:<texture>`
* `[verticalframe:<t>:<n>`
* `[mask:<texture>`
* `[sheet:<w>x<h>:<x>,<y>`
* `[colorize:<color>:<ratio>`
* `[colorizehsl:<hue>:<saturation>:<lightness>`
* `[multiply:<color>`
* `[screen:<color>`
* `[hsl:<hue>:<saturation>:<lightness>`
* `[contrast:<contrast>:<brightness>`
* `[overlay:<file>`
* `[hardlight:<file>`
* `[png:<base64 data>`

**Escaping:** modifiers that take texture names (e.g. `[combine`) accept
backslash escapes, required for `^`, `:` and `\`.
* `cobble.png^[lowpart:50:color.png\^[mask\:trans.png`
* As a Lua string: `"cobble.png^[lowpart:50:color.png\\^[mask\\:trans.png"`
]]
---@alias core.Texture string